    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "**Setting Up**\n\nThe whole workflow splits into 2 parts, one for inputting the data directly into 2 separate n8n data tables and the other part runs on a scheduled timer that creates a database page in the notion\n \nHow to setup Notion Unit:\n1. Create two data tables in N8N, one will be used for recording purchases (Create 3 Headers in the table schema: Cost, Expenditure_name and date). The other table is used for recording events and activities (Create 3 Headers: Journal_entry, timing and date)\n\n2. Create a Notion Database page\n \n3. Setting up the Notion Credentials. Login to the notion developer  portal, go into connections from the notion developer tools page. Request for the  API (IMPT: Make sure you add the page the database is stored in under the API's content access)\n\n4. Configure the create N8N Database node to \"create\", \"Database Page\", select the database page that you have given N8N access to\n\n5. Setup the Gemini Credentials with the API key that can be generated from Google AI studio, choose whichever model works best for your use (Other AI providers can be used by switching the AI agent host node)\n\n6. Configure the schedule trigger to occur at any specific timing (IMPT: Configure your N8N instance to match the local region .e.g New York/America\n\nHow to Setup Telegram and Data Entry unit\n\n1. Create a new telegram bot from Botfather, copy and paste the bot token into the telegram credentials then verify \n\n2. Configure the AI models if has not been done previously\n",
